Day 23 – PHP Strings & Operators
 What I Learned :
On Day 23, I learned how PHP strings and operators work together to process data and make decisions on the server side.
These concepts are critical because most user input and security logic depend on them.
 
PHP Strings :

Strings are used to handle:
Usernames
Passwords
Messages
URLs

 Basic Example :
<?php
$name = "Chinna";
echo "Welcome " . $name;
?>

 PHP Operators :
Operators control logic and comparisons.

 Common Operators :
Arithmetic: + - * /
Comparison: == != >= <= ===
Logical: && || !

 Example :
<?php
$age = 20;

if ($age >= 18) {
    echo "Access Allowed";
} else {
    echo "Access Denied";
}
?>

Security Notes :

Strings are common targets for injection attacks
Use strict comparison (===)
Always validate and sanitize string input

 Key Takeaway :

Strings carry data,Operators decide trust.
